WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.970
RMF is closely associated with NIST guidance.

00:00:02.970 --> 00:00:08.055
NIST Special Publication 800-37 describes the Risk Management Framework process and how

00:00:08.055 --> 00:00:11.250
organizations can apply it to information systems and organizations.

00:00:11.250 --> 00:00:15.915
NIST Special Publication 800-53 is commonly associated with the security and privacy

00:00:15.915 --> 00:00:17.385
controls used in RMF.

00:00:17.385 --> 00:00:21.840
It provides a catalog of controls that organizations can select and tailor based on system

00:00:21.840 --> 00:00:22.480
impact,

00:00:22.480 --> 00:00:25.465
risk context, mission needs, and organizational requirements.

00:00:25.465 --> 00:00:29.400
Other NIST publications and organizational policies may support categorization,

00:00:29.400 --> 00:00:33.570
assessment, continuous monitoring, privacy risk management, system security planning,

00:00:33.570 --> 00:00:34.945
and control implementation.

00:00:34.945 --> 00:00:38.120
RMF often sits within a broader governance ecosystem.

00:00:38.120 --> 00:00:38.800
In practice,

00:00:38.800 --> 00:00:43.665
NIST guidance helps teams move from abstract risk concerns to concrete control decisions.

00:00:43.665 --> 00:00:45.635
Instead of saying a system should be secure,

00:00:45.635 --> 00:00:49.190
RMF helps teams define which controls are relevant, how they will be implemented,

00:00:49.190 --> 00:00:51.360
and how evidence will show that they are working.

00:00:51.360 --> 00:00:54.549
The control catalog is not meant to be copied blindly.

00:00:54.549 --> 00:00:58.720
Organizations select and tailor controls based on the system, data, environment, threats,

00:00:58.720 --> 00:01:01.280
mission, law, policy, and risk tolerance.

00:01:01.280 --> 00:01:05.020
This tailoring is one reason RMF is a risk management framework rather than only a

00:01:05.020 --> 00:01:05.785
checklist.

00:01:05.785 --> 00:01:08.285
NIST also emphasizes ongoing risk management.

00:01:08.285 --> 00:01:13.150
The framework includes preparation, categorization, selection, implementation, assessment,

00:01:13.150 --> 00:01:14.075
authorization,

00:01:14.075 --> 00:01:17.600
and continuous monitoring because systems and environments change over time.

00:01:17.600 --> 00:01:21.230
For learners, the important point is that RMF gives structure to risk management.

00:01:21.230 --> 00:01:24.560
NIST publications provide the common vocabulary and process model,

00:01:24.560 --> 00:01:28.800
while each organization applies that model to its own systems and responsibilities.

00:01:28.800 --> 00:01:31.440
This common vocabulary matters in large organizations.

00:01:31.440 --> 00:01:34.150
It allows security, privacy, engineering, operations,

00:01:34.150 --> 00:01:37.640
and leadership teams to discuss controls and risk with less ambiguity.
